## 🐛 Describe the bug

With E+PD routing (#3153), a request whose selected serving pod has encoders in its roleset should run the encode stage before it is forwarded (`docs/source/features/gateway-routing/pd-disaggregation.rst:349`). When `requestsInflight` is positive and the request takes the multi-candidate path, it does not: `selectTargetPod` returns straight from `routeWithEarlyAdmission` (`pkg/plugins/gateway/gateway.go:957-958` at `8e96742`), so the `encodeMedia` call after `router.Route` (line 962) is never reached. Routing still succeeds and a serving pod is selected; only the encoder call is skipped.

The same request is encoded when the cap is unset, or when there is a single serving pod (that path has its own `encodeMedia` call). The cap branch came in with #3159, after E+PD support in #3153.

Because serving pods can encode missing outputs themselves (`pd-disaggregation.rst:334`), responses stay correct; what is lost is the encode offload. I have not measured latency or GPU load.

## Steps to Reproduce

From the repository root at `8e96742`, put this file in `pkg/plugins/gateway/` and run `go test ./pkg/plugins/gateway -run TestEPlusPDEncodesWithInflightLimit -count=1 -v`. It routes one image request through `selectTargetPod` with an encoder plus one or two serving pods, and counts requests that reach the encoder:

